t="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I655acbf8783f16d768cc24e36a7a9e68f1b69b41" commit="dc2d22d26b02b095fff4a4d26e2d89310d434045" commit_message="login: Add EmitArcBooted D-Bus method  to allow Chrome to send arc-booted Upstart signal.  Currently, the signal is sent by /etc/init/arc-boot-watcher.conf like this:   script    [...]    while ! /usr/sbin/android-sh -c 'getprop sys.boot_completed' | grep 1 ;    do      sleep 1    done    initctl emit arc-booted  end script  but as you can see, it's based on a polling and is not very clean. With this CL, we can remove the Upstart hack.  BUG=b:31254747 TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=cyan --packages chromeos-login TEST=cros_run_unit_tests --board=rambi --packages chromeos-login TEST='grep arc-booted /var/log/messages' on a device CQ-DEPEND=CL:384616  Change-Id: I655acbf8783f16d768cc24e36a7a9e68f1b69b41 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384594 Commit-Ready: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="384594" owner_email="yusukes@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/94/384594/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="3"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I185fdf6ba7565633f8b2cbdfe556a49da436ebb8" commit="21029c3f331552d7bd091370de43bd7ba9162656" commit_message="secure_less.sh: fix user flag to sudo  We need the -u flag to come before the command otherwise sudo passes that down as the argument to the command (and thus never actually drops root permissions).  BUG=None TEST=ran secure_less.sh and checked that `less` was nobody and not root  Change-Id: I185fdf6ba7565633f8b2cbdfe556a49da436ebb8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/384413 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger 